1acfef97c3b3"],

Cell["\<\
In the following we show how an impulse response function, h, is convolved \
with an input signal, x, to produce the output, y. In this demo you can \
select the input to be Gaussian white noise, a unit step or a unit area \
impulse. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.795792637159613*^9, 3.795793460878191*^9}, {
   3.795793497478001*^9, 3.795793876154686*^9}, {3.795793916938582*^9, 
   3.795793966336678*^9}, {3.795794001200252*^9, 3.7957940824750032`*^9}, {
   3.795796053815051*^9, 3.795796074506651*^9}, {3.795796111797822*^9, 
